{"event": "report", "t": 1795122146.157, "claim": "fixed", "text": "The deprecation error is fixed. The project compiles cleanly (exit 0), and the compiled SQL hashes nulls as empty strings, as the old macro did.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- **`dbt_project.yml`**: added `vars: surrogate_key_treat_nulls_as_empty_strings: true`. This is the flag the warning asks for. It keeps the new macro's hashing identical to the old `surrogate_key`, so existing `DATE_SENTIMENT_ID` and `LISTING_HOST_ID` values don't change for the incremental `unique_key`s.\n- **Switched `dbt_utils.surrogate_key` to `dbt_utils.generate_surrogate_key`** in all five models that called the removed macro:\n  - `models/agg/monthly_agg_reviews.sql` (the model in your error)\n  - `models/agg/daily_agg_reviews.sql`\n  - `models/agg/mom_agg_reviews.sql`\n  - `models/agg/wow_agg_reviews.sql`\n  - `models/dim/dim_listings_hosts.sql` (same problem, found by searching the project)\n\n**Verification**\n\n- A grep finds no remaining `dbt_utils.surrogate_key` calls in `models/` or `macros/`.\n- `dbt compile` exits 0. The only output is an existing warning about two unused seed config paths, which I left alone.\n\nI only compiled the models. I did not run them against the warehouse, so the incremental runs are unverified.\n\nVERDICT: fixed"}
